### Equivalence with `main`

A differential run compared `main` with this branch over 66 images: real photos and wallpapers; generated JPEG and PNG at 2047, 2048, and 2049 px; 4032x3024 at 9.1 MB and 43.8 MB; 1x3000 and 3000x1; transparent, palette, 16-bit, and grayscale PNG; progressive, CMYK, and EXIF-oriented JPEG; static, transparent, and animated WebP; static and animated GIF; BMP, TIFF, AVIF, and HEIC; and truncated, scrambled, zero-byte, and misnamed files. It used 11 `loadWebMedia` option sets (byte caps from 64 KiB to 6 MiB, quality policies, model side and pixel limits, image counts) and 7 direct `optimizeImageBufferForWebMedia` parameter sets with 4 content type and file name variants. The same source bytes were requested under different settings in one process, in forward, reverse, and shuffled order with heavy LRU eviction.

| Check | Compared | Differences |
| --- | ---: | ---: |
| `loadWebMedia` / `optimizeImageBufferForWebMedia`: sha256, length, content type, kind, file name, error class and message | 19,902 | 0 |
| Undecodable inputs, isolated per process | 428 | 0 |
| Tiny caps (700 B to 4 KB), including over-cap errors, never cached | 84 | 0 |
| Callers zero-filling returned buffers, then reloading | 42 | 0 |
| `hydratePromptMediaMessages` on persisted turns, 3 times per image, with workspace, explicit, and default roots; plus `materializeProviderContext` | 2,856 | 0 |

`main` itself was deterministic in all 2,922 same-process repeat pairs, which is what makes caching the encode safe.

### Tests

- `src/media/web-media.test.ts` "keys reused encodes by the byte cap and keeps them isolated from caller edits": reuses an encode under one cap, zero-fills the returned buffers, then checks that the next reuse and a tighter cap both equal a fresh encode. It fails if the cap is left out of the key, or if the cache hands out or stores a buffer without copying it.
- `src/agents/embedded-agent-runner/run/images.replay.test.ts` "encodes an oversized stored photo once across replayed model requests": hydrates a persisted turn with a 2200 px photo three times. The content must be identical and the image processor must encode once. A `vi.mock` wrapper counts encodes and delegates to the real processor, the same pattern `tool-images.test.ts` uses for #167355. It fails on `main` (3 encodes) and when replay loads without reuse.
- `pnpm test <file> --maxWorkers=1` wall time: `src/media/web-media.test.ts` 26.3 s (the new test 0.52 s), `src/agents/embedded-agent-runner/run/images.replay.test.ts` 14.7 s (the new test 0.06 s).

